### ============================================================
### Admin: Data Quality — Pillar 1 (Measure), issue #319
###
### Read-only. Nothing here changes an event; the fixing happens through
### events.http's `PUT /api/admin/events/{id}`, which is the point of the
### worklist below.
### ============================================================

### The report — per-source metrics plus an overall roll-up
### Computed live against the current table, so it always describes now.
### For trends, read the daily `data_quality_snapshot` rows or the
### `data_quality{source=…,metric=…}` Prometheus gauges instead: a
### point-in-time report cannot show whether anything moved.
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### The worklist — the events failing one metric, so they can be fixed
### The headline gap: CONCERT events with nothing in the lineup.
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/worklist?issue=concertsWithoutArtist
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Worklist for one source only
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/worklist?issue=concertsWithoutArtist&source=badehaus
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Worklist for hand-created events
### `manual` is the synthetic bucket for events with no `event_source_id` —
### they are reported rather than filtered out, so the report's own total
### agrees with the table's.
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/worklist?issue=missingGenre&source=manual
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Worklist, paged
### `limit` is capped at 500. Ordered newest-first by event date with the id
### as a tie-break, so a page boundary is stable across requests.
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/worklist?issue=missingPrice&limit=20&offset=20
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

