### What the import's sync gate kept out of each event
### An artist name it refused or held back, or a genre value it dropped (#320). Each
### entry's `flags` names the kind and the value; the next import replaces them.
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/worklist?issue=flaggedAtImport
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### An unknown issue is a 400 naming the valid values — NOT an empty list
### An empty list is the honest answer to "this metric has no offenders", so
### returning it for a typo would report perfect data quality for a metric
### that does not exist.
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/worklist?issue=missingArtist
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 400", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "Expected 400 but got " + response.status);
    });
    client.test("names the valid values", function () {
        client.assert(/concertsWithoutArtist/.test(response.body.detail || ""),
            "The 400 should list the metrics that do exist, was: " + JSON.stringify(response.body));
    });
%}

### The gauges the same numbers publish, for Prometheus
### Not reachable on `importer-host`: actuator lives on the management port
### (9001 in the chart, 8081's sibling locally), which no Ingress routes.
### Locally: curl http://localhost:8081/actuator/prometheus | grep data_quality

### ============================================================
### Suggestions — Pillar 4's proposals, issue #474
###
### A check proposes a fix with its evidence; a person decides. Nothing here
### writes to an event: apply a fix with events.http's
### `PUT /api/admin/events/{id}`, which pins the field.
### ============================================================

### Open suggestions, newest first
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/suggestions?status=OPEN
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
    if (response.body.content.length > 0) {
        client.global.set("suggestionId", response.body.content[0].id);
    }
%}

### The suggestions for one event
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/suggestions?eventId=1
Accept: application/json

### Dismiss one — run the list above first. A second dismissal is a no-op;
### an accepted suggestion answers 409, an unknown id 404.
POST {{importer-host}}/api/admin/data-quality/suggestions/{{suggestionId}}/dismiss
Accept: application/json
